---
const terms = [
  ["Noun", "A person, place, thing or idea", "dog, city, happiness"],
  ["Pronoun", "A word that replaces a noun", "he, she, it, they"],
  ["Antecedent", "The noun a pronoun refers to", "Tom lost <strong>his</strong> pencil. Tom is the antecedent."],
  ["Agreement", "The pronoun matches the noun in number and gender", "The girls took <strong>their</strong> bags."]
];
const examples = [
  ["Each student must bring <strong>his or her</strong> book.", "Each student is singular, so the pronoun is singular."],
  ["All the boys brought <strong>their</strong> lunches.", "Boys is plural, so the pronoun is their."],
  ["The cat licked <strong>its</strong> paw.", "Cat is singular and not a person, so the pronoun is its."],
  ["If a person wants to succeed, <strong>he or she</strong> must try hard.", "Person is singular."],
  ["The children did <strong>their</strong> homework before <strong>they</strong> played.", "Children is plural, so the pronouns are their and they."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Noun and Pronoun Agreement - What it is</h1>
  <p>
    A pronoun must agree with its noun in <strong>number</strong> (singular or plural) and <strong>person</strong> (who is speaking, or who is being spoken about). The noun a pronoun refers to is its <strong>antecedent</strong>.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-sand">
    <h2>Words to know</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <colgroup>
        <col class="concept" />
        <col class="practise" />
        <col class="example" />
      </colgroup>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Term</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Meaning</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          terms.map(([term, meaning, example]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{term}</th>
              <td>{meaning}</td>
              <td set:html={example} />
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <div class="trap-card trap-compact">
    <section class="trap">
      <h2>Match the number</h2>
      <p>
        The boy lost <strong>his</strong> hat.
        <span class="mark mark-yes" aria-label="Correct">✓</span>
        <em>Boy</em> is singular, so the pronoun is <strong>his</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The boy lost <strong>their</strong> hat.
        <span class="mark mark-no" aria-label="Incorrect">✕</span>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Match the pronoun to the noun</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Example</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Why</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          examples.map(([example, why]) => (
            <tr>
              <td set:html={example} />
              <td>{why}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</div>
